text:
{
  "errors": [
    {
      "span": "Om, and from the specific attribute, Om.",
      "category": "accuracy",
      "severity": "critical"
    },
    {
      "span": "Whoever knows the imperishable Brahman, which is the bridge for the wise, that is the Supreme.",
      "category": "accuracy",
      "severity": "critical"
    },
    {
      "span": "It is not possible to describe its qualities separately due to its infinite nature.",
      "category": "accuracy",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "span": "Therefore, the term ‘Brahman’ serves to encompass all.",
      "category": "accuracy",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "span": "Hence, this term ‘Brahman’ is specifically an attribute of Vishnu.",
      "category": "accuracy",
      "severity": "critical"
    },
    {
      "span": "For, the qualities are infinite, and from whom the others are not distinct, that is the imperishable, all-pervading one.",
      "category": "accuracy",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "span": "Thus it is stated in the Brahma Upanishad.",
      "category": "terminology",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "span": "Nor is the identity (samanyo) of the individual soul (jiva) with the Supreme Self (Atman) asserted.",
      "category": "accuracy",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "span": "The Self is true, the individual soul is true, the distinction is true, the distinction is true, the distinction is true. I shall not ascend, I shall not ascend, I shall not ascend.",
      "category": "accuracy",
      "severity": "critical"
    },
    {
      "span": "Thus it is stated in the Paingira Shruiti.",
      "category": "terminology",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "span": "For, the Self is the Supreme, independent, and possessing superior qualities, whereas the individual soul is of limited power, dependent, and inferior.",
      "category": "accuracy",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "span": "Thus it is stated in the Bhalleya Shruiti.",
      "category": "terminology",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "span": "Just as the distinction between the Lord (Ishvara) and the individual soul (jiva) is true by definitive conclusion, so too, you are fit to speak my true words here.",
      "category": "accuracy",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "span": "Just as the Lord and the individual soul are truly distinct from each other, may the gods, along with the companions of Kesava, protect me with that truth.",
      "category": "accuracy",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "span": "Thus, and so on, the distinction is not false.",
      "category": "fluency",
      "severity": "minor"
    }
  ]
}
